From f7211c04a846fc2c1095fdc97c6cb9eeb04fc200 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josep Torra <n770galaxy@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 18:20:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] drm/gma500: boot the SGX545 microkernel on Cedarview

Add dri/N/sgx/boot. It runs the DDK's first power-on sequence: clock
gating, init script part 1, the hardware-recovery reset with the EDM page
directory in BIF directory list 15, init script part 2, then the boot kick on
EVENT_KICK2, and polls HostCtl for INIT_COMPLETE. The register order lives in
sgx_seq.c behind callbacks and is pinned by a KUnit test. dri/N/sgx/status
dumps the registers and control blocks, dri/N/sgx/stop runs the deinit script
and holds the core in reset, and unload stops it before freeing its memory.

The ukernel goes at the start of the code heap: its branch targets and the
CCB service addresses are instruction indices from the EDM code base. While
the firmware runs, gma500's SGX interrupt handler no longer clears the
firmware's events; only the software event is acknowledged.

On a GMA3600 (SGX545 1.0.13) the EDM reports init complete 140 us after the
kick and then ticks at 1 kHz.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Josep Torra <n770galaxy@gmail.com>
